#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:5
#: 0d45286b39174a2bac0035149f17ae48
msgid "Connecting as a Support Engineer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:7
#: 50f02282220746debc5e2a5072a39568
msgid "this page is for the use of ArduPilot support engineers. If you are a Partner or user, see :ref:`support_proxy` for instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:10
#: b3a63527fadb41faad855d28dedd30bc
msgid "If you are a support engineer you will have been given 3 pieces of information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:13
#: a9d3d35293db4870b983ea93b3f9c8cf
msgid "the port number that you will connect on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:14
#: f4cbea5f72f84909812ac5bc41db4967
msgid "the port number that your users will connect on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:15
#: 0cd575bc3c7d48bd811fcc861a42cf11
msgid "an initial randomly generated MAVLink2 signing pass phrase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:19
#: 5228b2baf1ca4255b5a8fb9c36303651
msgid "Your computers system clock must be accurate for the proxy to work. If it is off by more than one minute then signing may fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:22
#: 9e0f2acf219041adabd1dcb1214b6368
msgid "To setup your support proxy port for MissionPlanner you need to use the Advanced->Mavlink Signing tool:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:28
#: a75064e2a4c146cd965bd7df02a6371a
msgid "In that tool you need to create a signing key using the pass phrase you have been given:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:34
#: 23998970a4ed419c97d1f4bfcd20e014
msgid "Use the \"Add\" button to add the key, and the \"Save\" button to save it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:36
#: 03f285c0437848a4b630e3849447eba6
msgid "Once the signing key is setup you can start to accept connections from users. You should direct your users to the instructions at the top of this page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:40
#: 4d78121229054bac96588c0681c29106
msgid "To connect to your side of the proxy use a TCP or UDPCI connection method in MissionPlanner:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:46
#: 08447f2ec0414144bb5058c562157881
msgid "After pressing connect choose \"support.ardupilot.org\" as the host:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:51
#: eb19abebef0d46e2b75a99ef2e398e2a
msgid "and your support engineer port number as the port:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:57
#: ed98672272f7402b890dabeff2e75108
msgid "Managing Your Connection with the Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:59
#: 8523d15bd6ab45fba656e6ab6c516d60
msgid "The proxy has a web dashboard at `support.ardupilot.org/dashboard <https://support.ardupilot.org/dashboard>`__. Log in there with your **support engineer port number** and your current pass phrase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:66
#: 03455d7dc1874141a251e6751006322c
msgid "From the dashboard you can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:68
#: 6c984b3475b84b2ab1c9e043a1018fd1
msgid "change the MAVLink2 signing pass phrase for your connection (use the \"Generate\" button to get a fresh random one, or type your own, then \"Save\"). This is the easiest way to rotate the pass phrase — it takes effect on the proxy immediately. The Mission Planner method below still works if you prefer it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:73
#: 2411ba42261a4c10ae636616d83fc20a
msgid "see which user and support-engineer connections are live right now (peer addresses, byte counts, link health), and drop a stuck connection if needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:76
#: f23a067562fb46c397a59d9587592494
msgid "optionally record the session: tick \"record telemetry logs\" to capture a MAVProxy-format ``.tlog`` of the session, and/or \"record ArduPilot bin logs\" to capture the vehicle's dataflash log over MAVLink as a ``.bin`` (the firmware must have the MAVLink logging backend enabled). Recorded logs are listed on the dashboard and can be downloaded there; a per-connection retention period controls how long they are kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:84
#: 4f496c8af3f84ad3bc77259c8de05e4d
msgid "ArduPilot partners with admin access can additionally manage every connection from the dashboard and create new partner connections (including a block of consecutive IDs in one step)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:88
#: a84b541e16af4db0a2319774163429a6
msgid "To change the pass phrase from Mission Planner instead, create and save a new key in the MAVLink Signing tool then select it and press the \"Use\" button:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:95
#: 0941567a38694feabf70b5898142f371
msgid "pressing \"Use\" will update the signing key for your support ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:97
#: 0d3d49f388024ad98d9bf22aca87f6ba
msgid "If your stored signing timestamp gets ahead of your computer's clock (for example after a clock change) signing can start failing with a replay rejection. On the dashboard's edit page, tick \"reset signing timestamp\" and Save to recover; if you don't have dashboard access, ask for the timestamp to be reset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:103
#: aa3be86b58d64651b457e2addc9d9040
msgid "For technical support please contact Andrew Tridgell on your partner support channel on discord."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:107
#: 80aaaf15d4184839a5b62f9d06e1fc21
msgid "Useful Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:109
#: 732e26d97ab34f97b3d53a1780e7f763
msgid "When helping a user with remote tuning, having them run this `LUA Applet <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/applets/revert_param.md>`__ to allow you to instantly revert all tuning in case of an issue, may be useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:112
#: f95152b5a3d24dcd9bcf12f155c3c4c1
msgid "Using MAVProxy as a Support Engineer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:114
#: bb272c0ec31b4389adf0b711281fa320
msgid "An example shell script for connecting as a support engineer using MAVProxy is `available here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/SupportProxy/blob/main/mav_support.sh>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:118
#: b9efadcd82ea4ba1b3a9289eb747966c
msgid "DroneCAN GUI Tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:120
#: e12272c7f6ee45c5beb025e1600b0c53
msgid "Enter \"mavcan:udpout:support.ardupilot.org:\" followed by your support engineer port number for the CAN interface and add your signing key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/support_proxy_supportengineer.rst:122
#: d17fc016a1b44a3bb0acc0632025a709
msgid "The signing key in DroneCAN GUI Tool is the password entered into Mission Planner during key generation. It is not the key that Mission Planner displays."
msgstr ""

